  "source_rationale": "A difference binding combined with an absolute (point) temperature follows the Ruby source scale transitions: difference plus point is a point in the kernel reference unit, and difference minus point is a difference, not a ScaleOperationError. Each row names the scale24 source row with the same operands, units and difference flags (an absent flag is false); the kernel value equals that row's value. The legacy files stay byte for byte; these rows pin each legacy expectation and give the source-governed one.",
